Package: costas
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: Costas contributors <https://github.com/somedudenamedtony/costas/issues>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: wsjtx, libhamlib-utils, libportaudio2, libfontconfig1, libx11-6, libice6, libsm6, ca-certificates
Recommends: libsecret-tools, pulseaudio-utils
Section: hamradio
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://somedudenamedtony.github.io/costas/
Description: station-centric digital modes client for amateur radio
 Costas operates FT8, FT4, PSK31, PSK63 and RTTY. It decodes FT8 and FT4 with
 the jt9 decoder from WSJT-X and controls the radio through Hamlib's rigctld,
 then shows one line per station: who you still need, who is free to call and
 who can hear you.
 .
 This is a preview of the Linux version.
